# SYNTAX TEST "Packages/Carve/Carve.sublime-syntax"

# Snippet definitions and uses (C2-B-236, C2-I-128, C2-B-237), sublime-carve#115.

{$ver}: 0.2.3
# <- meta.snippet.definition.carve punctuation.definition.snippet.begin.carve
#^ punctuation.definition.snippet.begin.carve
# ^^^ variable.other.snippet.carve
#    ^ punctuation.definition.snippet.end.carve
#     ^ punctuation.separator.carve
#^^^^^^^^^^^^ meta.snippet.definition.carve
#^^^^^^^^^^^^ -meta.attributes.carve

Release {{ $ver }} of the tool, with *strong* after.
#       ^^^^^^^^^^ meta.snippet.use.carve
#       ^^ punctuation.definition.snippet.begin.carve
#          ^^^^ variable.other.snippet.carve
#               ^^ punctuation.definition.snippet.end.carve
#       ^^^^^^^^^^ -meta.directive.include.carve
#                                    ^^^^^^^^ markup.bold.carve

{{ $ver }}
# <- meta.snippet.use.carve punctuation.definition.snippet.begin.carve
#^^^^^^^^^ meta.snippet.use.carve
#^^^^^^^^^ -meta.directive.include.carve
#  ^^^^ variable.other.snippet.carve

Text after the block use with *strong*.
#                             ^^^^^^^^ markup.bold.carve

A use alone on its line is a one-line block, so a list can follow it.

{{ $ver }}
- item
# <- punctuation.definition.list.begin.carve

{$v .k :en}{.c}: value *b*
# <- meta.snippet.definition.carve
#  ^^^^^^^ meta.snippet.definition.carve meta.attributes.carve
#   ^^ entity.other.attribute-name.class.carve
#      ^^^ entity.other.attribute-name.language.carve
#         ^ punctuation.definition.snippet.end.carve
#          ^^^^ meta.snippet.definition.carve meta.attributes.carve
#           ^^ entity.other.attribute-name.class.carve
#              ^ punctuation.separator.carve
#                      ^^^ meta.snippet.definition.carve markup.bold.carve

An id in the marker defines nothing.

{$v #x}: a
# <- -meta.snippet.definition.carve
# ^ -variable.other.snippet.carve

No space before the value defines nothing.

{$v}:x
# <- -meta.snippet.definition.carve
# ^ -variable.other.snippet.carve

A definition-shaped lazy line of an open paragraph is text:
{$v}: a
# <- -meta.snippet.definition.carve
# ^ -variable.other.snippet.carve

- item
{$v}: a
# <- -meta.snippet.definition.carve
# ^ -variable.other.snippet.carve

- item

  {$v}: a
# ^ -meta.snippet.definition.carve
#   ^ -variable.other.snippet.carve

Glued blocks after a use stay text: A {{ $v }}{.c} b
#                                     ^^^^^^^^ meta.snippet.use.carve
#                                             ^^^^ -meta.attributes.carve

No pads {{$v}} make no use.
#       ^^^^^^ -meta.snippet.use.carve
#         ^^ -variable.other.snippet.carve

Escaped \{{ $v }} is text.
#        ^^^^^^^^ -meta.snippet.use.carve
#           ^^ -variable.other.snippet.carve

{{ "a {{ $v }}.crv" }}
# <- punctuation.definition.directive.begin.carve
#      ^^^^^^^^ -meta.snippet.use.carve
#         ^^ -variable.other.snippet.carve

{{ $a.crv }}
# <- punctuation.definition.directive.begin.carve
#  ^^^^^^ string.other.link.include.carve
#  ^^^^^^ -meta.snippet.use.carve

{{ $v @shift:1 }}
# <- punctuation.definition.directive.begin.carve
#  ^^ string.other.link.include.carve
#     ^^^^^^ variable.parameter.include.carve
#  ^^ -meta.snippet.use.carve

{{ path.crv }}
# <- punctuation.definition.directive.begin.carve
#  ^^^^^^^^ string.other.link.include.carve

An attribute line directly above a block use is not taken by it (carve#6896).
The line is paragraph text; an assertion line between the two would end the
shape, so only the use below is asserted here.

{.k :en}
{{ $v }}
# <- meta.snippet.use.carve
#^^^^^^^ meta.snippet.use.carve
